<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Diepholz</h1><p class="st-meta">1085 CE – 1585 CE (approx.) · capital Diepholz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Lower Saxon county of moors and lakes south of Bremen, held by the noble lords of Diepholz until their line died out in 1585.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of Diepholz are first recorded around 1085 as noble lords on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunte">Hunte</a> river, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen">Bremen</a>. Their territory lay among moors around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dummer">Dümmer</a> lake, with a castle at Diepholz controlling a route across the marshes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lords, later counts from 1531, ruled a small, poor territory of moorland villages. They were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of several overlords and balanced between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minden">Minden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a> and the dukes of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> was introduced in the 16th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When Count Friedrich II died without heirs in 1585, Diepholz passed by feudal right to the Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celle">Celle</a>, and later to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hanover">Electorate of Hanover</a>. It is now part of the district of Diepholz in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1085 CE – 1585 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="